## =====================================================================
## PCIe-6351 bring-up - a2d and d2a through the NI-DAQmx backend
## =====================================================================
##
## A deliberately tiny scan (5 traces, a couple of seconds) for proving a
## new card end to end before trusting it with a real measurement.
##
## BEFORE RUNNING THIS, CHECK WHAT IS WIRED TO ao0. The d2a block below
## drives a real voltage out of it. If a mirror, piezo or amplifier is
## connected, confirm -1..+1 V is safe for it, or comment the block out -
## the a2d half of this file is useful on its own.
##
## Run it in this order:
##
##   pydaq list                 -> does pscan see the card at all?
##   pscan --dry-run examples/bringup_6351.con
##   pscan --timer  examples/bringup_6351.con
##
## --timer is the point of this file. It breaks each trace down so you can
## see what the committed DAQmx task actually costs per coordinate on your
## kernel, rather than taking an estimate for it.
##
## Expected output: bringup_6351_a2d1_1f.d, 5 traces x 1000 samples of
## float32 volts = 20000 bytes. Reload in MATLAB the same way as any other
## .d file; the backend makes no difference to the format.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------
## One trace per coordinate. Raise this to average at a point.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------
action count
count 1
end

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------
## The output axis: sweeps ao0 over -1..+1 V in 0.5 V steps (5 points).
##
## 'device Dev1' is whatever 'pydaq list' reported - NI assigns the
## name, it is not a /dev node. Drop the line to auto-detect, which works
## as long as only one card can serve the block.
##
## 'settle 0.01' is a guess. A galvo settles in about a millisecond, a
## piezo in tens. Find the real number by raising it until the trace stops
## changing, then leave a little margin.
##
## 'restore' puts ao0 back to -1 V when the sweep finishes.
##
## Axis 98 rather than the default 99 for two reasons: 99 prints as
## "Z/piezo" in the log, which would be misleading here, and leaving 99
## free means the real piezo can be added later as the inner axis without
## renumbering this one.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------
action d2a
axis 98
backend daqmx
device Dev1
channel 0
units volts
scan -1.0 1.0 0.5
limits -2.0 2.0
settle 0.01
restore
end

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------
## The input: 1000 samples at 10 kHz off ai0, at every coordinate.
##
## 'v_min'/'v_max' rather than 'range <index>': the volts resolve to the
## narrowest range the card offers that contains them, and mean the same
## thing if this config is ever pointed at the old comedi card.
##
## 'terminal rse' is single-ended against ground. Use 'diff' if the
## photodiode is wired differentially - on a 6351 that halves the usable
## channel count, ai0 pairing with ai8.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------
action a2d
channel 0
backend daqmx
device Dev1
v_min -1.0
v_max 1.0
terminal rse
sample_rate 10000
n_samples 1000
end
